      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### watch → job → run → snapshot\n\n| Table | Concern | Lifecycle |\n|---|---|---|\n| `availability_watch` | **User intent** — POI (or one reservable), dates, cadence, triggers. | Created by the user/API. Status: `active` / `paused` / `done`. |\n| `availability_job` | **Scheduler state** — `next_run_at`, claim token, frozen `intent_payload`. **1:1 with watch.** | Service writes/updates this when a watch is created or edited. |\n| `availability_job_run` | **Append-only execution log** — one row per poll: `started` / `completed` / `failed`, `snapshot_count`, `duration_ms`, `error`. | Inserted every time the executor runs a claimed job. |\n| `availability_snapshot` | **Observed availability** — per `(reservable_id, target_date, observed_at)`. Linked to the run via `run_id`. | Inserted in bulk by the executor for each job run. |\n\n### How to drill\n\nClick a **watch_id** / **job_id** / **run_id** anywhere in the tables below to scope the whole dashboard. Clear a var (top bar) to widen back out. Use per-column filters inside each table for status / errors / etc.\n\n### Where else to look\n\n| Question | Dashboard |\n|---|---|\n| What did a single run write? Full payload. | **[Watch / Job Run Detail](/d/watch-job-run-detail)** — drill in via `run_id`. |\n| Reservable-centric: full history + last fetch + watches scoped to one reservable. | **[Reservable / Detail](/d/reservable-detail)**. |\n| POI-centric: linked reservables, coverage. | **[POI Detail](/d/poi-detail)**. |\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.0",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "About this dashboard",
